ks later, he displayed the sketch at a local exhibition. Several passengers recognised themselves and laughed at how serious they had looked. What had felt like wasted time became the subject of his most popular picture.\\n\\nQuestion: Why were the passengers impatient?\",\"hi\":\"Original Story 3: The Ferry Painter\\n\\nEvery morning, Dev crossed the river by ferry and sketched the changing light on the water. One foggy day, the ferry was delayed, and impatient passengers complained. Dev used the extra time to draw their blurred reflections in the cabin windows. Weeks later, he displayed the sketch at a local exhibition. Several passengers recognised themselves and laughed at how serious they had looked. What had felt like wasted time became the subject of his most popular picture.\\n\\nQuestion: Why were the passengers impatient?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Dev refused to show his sketch.\",\"hi\":\"Dev refused to show his sketch.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The exhibition opened late.\",\"hi\":\"The exhibition opened late.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The ferry was delayed by fog.\",\"hi\":\"The ferry was delayed by fog.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The river had dried up.\",\"hi\":\"The river had dried up.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Simple Passage Based on a Book or Story\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"b346373f-915c-4b6d-908e-1bbabc0bcc62\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Story 2: The Note in the Atlas\\n\\nWhile arranging returned books, librarian Farid found a note inside an old atlas: “Look where the river meets the road.” He first assumed it was a clue to hidden money, but the map showed no such place. Then he noticed a child waiting near the desk. She explained that the note was part of a geography game she had designed for her younger brother. Farid helped her replace the note and suggested adding