riginal Story 2: The Note in the Atlas\\n\\nWhile arranging returned books, librarian Farid found a note inside an old atlas: “Look where the river meets the road.” He first assumed it was a clue to hidden money, but the map showed no such place. Then he noticed a child waiting near the desk. She explained that the note was part of a geography game she had designed for her younger brother. Farid helped her replace the note and suggested adding page numbers so that the next clue would be easier to follow.\\n\\nQuestion: Which trait does Farid display at the end?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Jealousy\",\"hi\":\"Jealousy\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Carelessness\",\"hi\":\"Carelessness\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Suspicion only\",\"hi\":\"Suspicion only\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Helpfulness\",\"hi\":\"Helpfulness\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Simple Passage Based on a Book or Story\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"a89b8167-fbf3-4abc-a7ef-396660a3c83b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Story 4: The Envelope of Seeds\\n\\nNora received an unlabelled envelope of seeds from her aunt. Instead of planting all of them in one place, she divided them among four pots and changed only one condition in each: sunlight, water, soil or temperature. She kept notes for three weeks. Two pots produced similar shoots, one grew slowly and one did not sprout. Nora could not identify the plant yet, but she had learned which conditions helped the seeds begin to grow.\\n\\nQuestion: Why did Nora use four pots?\",\"hi\":\"Original Story 4: The Envelope of Seeds\\n\\nNora received an unlabelled envelope of seeds from her aunt. Instead of planting all of them in one place, she divided them among four pots and changed only one condition in each: sunlight, water, soil or temperature. She kept notes for three weeks. Two pots produced similar shoots, one grew slowly and one did not sprout. Nora could not identify the plant yet, but she had learned which conditions helped the seeds begin to grow.\\n\\nQuestion: Why did Nora use four pots?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"To compare how different conditions affected the seeds\",\"hi\":\"To compare how different conditions affected the seeds\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"To decorate four separate rooms\",\"hi\":\"To decorate four separate rooms\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"To give every seed a different label\",\"hi\":\"To give every seed a different label\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"To prevent herself from keeping notes\",\"hi\":\"To prevent herself from keeping notes\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Simple Passage Based on a Book or Story\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"a69c2434-d627-4fd1-8a60-01458f18464e\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Story 3: The Ferry Painter\\n\\nEvery morning, Dev crossed the river by ferry and sketched the changing light on the water. One foggy day, the ferry was delayed, and impatient passengers complained. Dev used the extra time to draw their blurred reflections in the cabin windows. Weeks later, he displayed the sketch at a local exhibition. Several passengers recognised themselves and laughed at how serious they had looked. What had felt like wasted time became the subject of his most popular picture.\\n\\nQuestion: What did Dev draw during the delay?\",\"hi\":\"Original Story 3: The Ferry Painter\\n\\nEvery morning, Dev crossed the river by ferry and sketched the changing light on the water. One foggy day, the ferry was delayed, and impatient passengers complained. Dev used the extra time to draw their blurred reflections in the cabin windows. Weeks later, he displayed the sketch at a local exhibition. Several passengers recognised themselves and laughed at how serious they had looked. What had felt like wasted time became the subject of his most popular picture.\\n\\nQuestion: What did Dev draw during the delay?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A new ferry engine\",\"hi\":\"A new ferry engine\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Passengers’ blurred reflections\",\"hi\":\"Passengers’ blurred reflections\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The exhibition building\",\"hi\":\"The exhibition building\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A map of the river\",\"hi\":\"A map of the river\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Simple Passage Based on a Book or Story\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"9ab5b86b-2f6b-47a2-96a1-cdaf78f70170\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Story 1: The Watchmaker’s Drawer\\n\\nLeena’s grandfather repaired watches in a narrow shop. One drawer was always locked, and Leena imagined that it held a rare gold watch. When her grandfather finally gave her the key, she found only broken springs, cracked glass and rusted gears. He explained that each piece came from a repair that had taught him something new. The drawer was valuable not because of what the pieces were worth, but because of the mistakes they helped him remember.\\n\\nQuestion: What was actually in the drawer?\",\"hi\":\"Original Story 1: The Watchmaker’s Drawer\\n\\nLeena’s grandfather repaired watches in a narrow shop. One drawer was always locked, and Leena imagined that it held a rare gold watch. When her grandfather finally gave her the key, she found only broken springs, cracked glass and rusted gears. He explained that each piece came from a repair that had taught him something new. The drawer was valuable not because of what the pieces were worth, but because of the mistakes they helped him remember.\\n\\nQuestion: What was actually in the drawer?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Damaged watch parts\",\"hi\":\"Damaged watch parts\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Completed customer orders\",\"hi\":\"Completed customer orders\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Jewellery for sale\",\"hi\":\"Jewellery for sale\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Family photographs\",\"hi\":\"Family photographs\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Simple Passage Based on a Book or Story\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"952228fd-0be8-41de-b93f-9a970c88afc9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Story 4: The Envelope of Seeds\\n\\nNora received an unlabelled envelope of seeds from her aunt. Instead of planting all of them in one place, she divided them among four pots and changed only one condition in each: sunlight, water, soil or temperature. She kept notes for three weeks. Two pots produced similar shoots, one grew slowly and one did not sprout. Nora could not identify the plant yet, but she had learned which conditions helped the seeds begin to grow.\\n\\nQuestion: What does the story suggest about useful investigation?\",\"hi\":\"Original Story 4: The Envelope of Seeds\\n\\nNora received an unlabelled envelope of seeds from her aunt. Instead of planting all of them in one place, she divided them among four pots and changed only one condition in each: sunlight, water, soil or temperature. She kept notes for three weeks. Two pots produced similar shoots, one grew slowly and one did not sprout. Nora could not identify the plant yet, but she had learned which conditions helped the seeds begin to grow.\\n\\nQuestion: What does the story suggest about useful investigation?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It must identify everything immediately.\",\"hi\":\"It must identify everything immediately.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It should avoid written records.\",\"hi\":\"It should avoid written records.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It can answer one question even when another remains open.\",\"hi\":\"It can answer one question even when an